From 21fd3c8bb79cfd29ceb54a8fe46acf7673ebaee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OOHehir <40183643+OOHehir@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:12:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/img-rogue: do not BUG on module unload when no devices
 were registered

pvr_init() no longer calls pvr_devices_register(), as the GPU comes from the
device tree, so pvr_devices stays NULL. pvr_exit() still calls
pvr_devices_unregister(), whose BUG_ON(!pvr_devices) then fires on every
unload of the module: on a systemd image, rc.pvr.service runs
"modprobe -r pvrsrvkm" at shutdown & every reboot ends in a kernel panic.

The path exists only when the driver is built as a module; the vendor
defconfig builds it in. Return early instead, as there is nothing to
unregister.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/starfive-tech/linux/pull/150]
Signed-off-by: OOHehir <40183643+OOHehir@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../img-rogue/services/server/env/linux/pvr_platform_drv.c    | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/services/server/env/linux/pvr_platform_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/services/server/env/linux/pvr_platform_drv.c
index 7f2628d57222..54d91728cecf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/services/server/env/linux/pvr_platform_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/services/server/env/linux/pvr_platform_drv.c
@@ -153,7 +153,9 @@ static void pvr_devices_unregister(void)
 #if defined(MODULE) && !defined(PVR_LDM_PLATFORM_PRE_REGISTERED)
 	unsigned int i;
 
-	BUG_ON(!pvr_devices);
+	/* pvr_init() no longer registers devices; they come from the DT */
+	if (!pvr_devices)
+		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < pvr_num_devices && pvr_devices[i]; i++)
 		platform_device_unregister(pvr_devices[i]);
